config BR2_PACKAGE_OPENIPC_BSEL
	bool "openipc-bsel"
	depends on BR2_arm
	help
	  A/B bank selector for boards whose stock bootloader picks which
	  kernel/rootfs bank to boot next (e.g. CADDX Ascent's "fpvboot" u-boot
	  command) by reading a small "BSEL" magic record out of an MTD
	  partition named "sel". Reimplements that same record format
	  (reverse-engineered from the stock ar_bsel binary) so an OpenIPC
	  image running on either bank can flip which bank boots next, without
	  needing the stock bootloader's own userspace tool or its rootfs.

	  Installs /usr/bin/openipc-bsel, CLI-compatible with the stock tool:
	    openipc-bsel check_flash      read current bank from "sel"
	    openipc-bsel check_cmdline    read fpvbsel=N from /proc/cmdline
	    openipc-bsel set 0|1          switch the next boot to bank 0/1

	  Currently enabled by hi3516cv6xx_fpv_caddx-ascent-lite's defconfig.
	  Not device-specific by construction (it locates the "sel" partition
	  by name rather than hardcoding a device), so any other board using
	  the same BSEL scheme could select it too.
